<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Create Evidence | WorkProof</title>
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    
    <style>
        /* Color Variables */
        :root {
            --bg-cream: #FDFBF7;
            --text-dark: #2D3A3A;
            --green-forest: #2E5A4A;
            --green-sage: #8DA999;
            --accent-light: #E8E5D8;
            --white: #FFFFFF;
        }

        body {
            font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
            background-color: var(--bg-cream);
            color: var(--text-dark);
            line-height: 1.6;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 2rem;
        }

        .wp-main {
            max-width: 900px;
            margin: 0 auto;
        }

        /* Header */
        .lesson-header h1 {
            color: var(--green-forest);
            font-size: 2.5rem;
        }

        .subtitle {
            color: #555;
            font-size: 1.1rem;
        }

        /* Concept Cards */
        .concept-grid {
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
            gap: 1.5rem;
            margin: 2rem 0;
        }

        .concept-card {
            padding: 1.5rem;
            border-radius: 8px;
            border: 1px solid var(--accent-light);
            background: var(--white);
        }

        .evidence-card {
            border-top: 4px solid var(--green-forest);
        }

        .verdict.success {
            color: var(--green-forest);
            font-weight: 600;
        }

        /* Table Styling */
        .table-wrapper { margin-top: 2rem; overflow-x: auto; }
        .comparison-table {
            width: 100%;
            border-collapse: collapse;
            background: var(--white);
        }

        .comparison-table th {
            background: var(--green-forest);
            color: var(--bg-cream);
            padding: 1rem;
            text-align: left;
        }

        .comparison-table td {
            padding: 1rem;
            border-bottom: 1px solid var(--accent-light);
        }

        .cert-tag {
            background: var(--accent-light);
            padding: 0.2rem 0.6rem;
            border-radius: 4px;
            font-size: 0.85rem;
        }

        /* Ladder Styling */
        .ladder-step {
            display: flex;
            align-items: flex-start;
            gap: 1.5rem;
            margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
        }

        .step-num {
            font-weight: 700;
            color: var(--green-sage);
            font-size: 1.5rem;
        }

        /* Callout Styling */
        .creation-callout {
            background: var(--green-forest);
            color: var(--bg-cream);
            padding: 2.5rem;
            border-radius: 12px;
            text-align: center;
            margin-top: 3rem;
        }

        /* Evidence Block Lesson Styles */
        .evidence-block-guide {
            background: var(--white);
            border: 1px solid var(--accent-light);
            border-radius: 12px;
            padding: 2.5rem;
            margin: 3rem 0;
        }

        .evidence-block-guide h2 {
            color: var(--green-forest);
            margin-bottom: 1rem;
        }

        .eb-grid {
           display: grid;
           grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
           gap: 1.5rem;
           margin-top: 1.5rem;
         }

         @media (max-width: 768px) {
      
        .eb-grid {
         grid-template-columns: 1fr;
          }
        }        
   
        .eb-item {
            background: var(--bg-cream);
            padding: 1.25rem;
            border-radius: 8px;
            border-left: 3px solid var(--green-sage);
        }

        .eb-item h4 {
            color: var(--green-forest);
            margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <main class="wp-main">
        <header class="lesson-header">
            <h1>Shift from <em>Claiming</em> to <em>Presenting</em></h1>
            <p class="subtitle">When conventional career paths fracture, momentum doesn't come from credentials. It comes from absolute, undeniable leverage. Let's pivot your recovery strategy.</p>
        </header>

        <section class="concept-grid">
            <div class="concept-card claim-card">
                <h3>The Stagnant Resume Claim</h3>
                <p class="statement">"I am a resilient professional seeking a fresh opportunity after a setback in my previous venture."</p>
                <div class="verdict"><strong>The Market Asks:</strong> "What is your risk profile?"</div>
            </div>
            <div class="concept-card evidence-card">
                <h3>The Turnaround WorkProof</h3>
                <p class="statement">"I performed a post-mortem on my failed logistics startup, isolated the unit-economic leak, and built a transparent capital-allocation model that protects margins under supply chain volatility."</p>
                <div class="verdict success"><strong>The Market Asks:</strong> "How soon can you implement this?"</div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Teaching the Evidence Block Section -->
        <section class="evidence-block-guide">
    <h2>Anatomy of Work</h2>

    <p>
        Create a standalone, verifiable module of work that demonstrates your
        knowledge, problem-solving ability, and professional execution without
        relying solely on traditional credentials.
    </p>

    <div class="eb-grid">

        <div class="eb-item">
            <h4>1. The Diagnostic Hook</h4>
            <p>Identify the problem, inefficiency, or opportunity that prompted your work.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="eb-item">
            <h4>2. The Artifact Core</h4>
            <p>Present the deliverable, such as code, documentation, research, templates, or designs.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="eb-item">
            <h4>3. The Scalable Output</h4>
            <p>Show how the solution can be reused, expanded, or applied to similar situations.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="eb-item">
            <h4>4. Supporting Evidence</h4>
            <p>Include screenshots, metrics, documentation, testing results, or before-and-after comparisons.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="eb-item">
            <h4>5. Business Impact</h4>
            <p>Explain how your work improved efficiency, reduced costs, solved a problem, or created measurable value.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="eb-item">
            <h4>6. Reflection & Future Improvements</h4>
            <p>Describe what you learned, what you would improve, and how the project could evolve over time.</p>
        </div>

    </div>
</section>

        <section class="lesson-section">
            <h2>Pivoting From Failure to Structural Asset Creation</h2>
            <p class="section-intro">Setbacks offer data. Convert historical friction points into high-value intellectual property that proves deep expertise:</p>
            
            <div class="table-wrapper">
                <table class="comparison-table">
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th>The Stalled Milestone (Traditional Path)</th>
                            <th>The Post-Failure Asset (Tangible Evidence)</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td><span class="cert-tag">Failed Project</span></td>
                            <td>Authored a comprehensive 15-page post-mortem diagnostic report detailing macroeconomic risk vectors and mitigation safeguards.</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><span class="cert-tag">Layoff / Job Loss</span></td>
                            <td>Engineered a fully documented automated production pipeline and training manual that reduced team onboarding overhead by 50%.</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><span class="cert-tag">Stalled Creative or Technical Portfolio</span></td>
                            <td>Released an open-source architectural template solving a recurring malfunction in infrastructure deployment.</td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="lesson-section">
            <h2>The Recovery</h2>
            <p class="section-intro">When structural failures disrupt traditional employment, continue building undeniable artifacts that prove your executive capacity.</p>
            
            <div class="ladder-container">
                <div class="ladder-step">
                    <span class="step-num">07</span>
                    <div class="step-content">
                        <h4>Architecting Resilient Frameworks</h4>
                        <p>Designing systems and diagnostic risk models that prevent systemic vulnerabilities from recurring.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="ladder-step">
                    <span class="step-num">06</span>
                    <div class="step-content">
                        <h4>Strategic Turnaround Execution</h4>
                        <p>Re-engineering broken practices, cutting waste, and restoring functional profitability.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="ladder-step">
                    <span class="step-num">05</span>
                    <div class="step-content">
                        <h4>Codifying Failure into Education</h4>
                        <p>Publishing detailed case studies, backlash, and analytical frameworks that guides staff on what structural pitfalls to avoid.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="ladder-step">
                    <span class="step-num">04</span>
                    <div class="step-content">
                        <h4>Transparent Public Disclosure</h4>
                        <p>Releasing your hard-earned insights and metrics into public repositories for peer validation.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="ladder-step">
                    <span class="step-num">03</span>
                    <div class="step-content">
                        <h4>Prototyping Recovery Solutions</h4>
                        <p>Building standalone models, diagnostic toolkits, or modular codebases that directly solve the pain points that caused prior friction.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="creation-callout">
            <div class="callout-text">
                <h2>Ready to turn a setback into an asset?</h2>
                <p>Instead of asking <em>"How do I explain what went wrong?"</em> ask <strong>"What system can I build out of this lesson?"</strong> Transform professional friction into a permanent, verifiable Portfolio.</p>
            </div>
        </section>
    </main>

</body>
</html>
